.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_DOGS_HALF_JOIN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_dogs_half_join
.Nd a half-join over partially ordered times for delta queries
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/dogs.h
.Ft dtfl_collection *
.Fn dtfl_dogs_half_join "dtfl_collection *stream" "dtfl_arranged *arr" "const dtfl_type *kt" "const dtfl_type *v1t" "const dtfl_type *out_type" "bool strict" "dtfl_half_join_output_fn output_func" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_dogs_half_join
is a binary equijoin that responds only to updates on its first input, the
building block of delta joins over partially ordered times.
Each streamed update is a record
.Va kt Ns Li || Ns Va v1t Ns Li ||time1 ,
carried at an initial time less or equal to the hoisted
.Va time1 .
For every
.Pq key , val2
in the arrangement
.Va arr
at a trace
.Va time2
that the comparison accepts against the initial time, the operator emits
.Fn output_func key val1 val2
at the joined time
.Pq Va time1 No join Va time2 ,
carried at the initial time, with the product of the two diffs.
The joined time is appended to the output record, whose record part is
.Va out_type ,
so a later operator can delay the update to it; chaining half-joins this
way builds a delta join.
.Pp
.Va strict
selects the total-order comparison: true compares
.Va time2
strictly less than the initial time, ignoring concurrent updates; false
compares less or equal, seeing them.
Under an AltNeu scope these are the two sides that make a pair of
concurrent updates interact exactly once.
.Va kt
and
.Va v1t
split the streamed record into its key and value; the hoisted
.Va time1
is the scope's time words that follow them.
.Pp
A
.Vt dtfl_half_join_output_fn
writes the output record bytes for a matched
.Pq key , val1 , val2
through
.Va out_rec ,
storing the length through
.Va out_len .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns a new
.Vt dtfl_collection
the caller frees with
.Fn dtfl_collection_free ,
or
.Dv NULL
with
.Dv DTFL_EALGEBRA
when the two diff classes do not multiply.
The caller still owns
.Va arr .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_delay_neu 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_extend 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_dogs_propose 3
.Sh STANDARDS
A C11 port of the dogsdogsdogs
.Pa src/operators/half_join.rs .
.Pp
The multi-worker capability-downgrade bookkeeping of the upstream operator
is reduced to a single-worker deferral; the total-order comparison that
decides which trace times join is reproduced exactly.
